 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the expiration of the\nmortgage recording tax imposed by the city of Yonkers",
    "basePrintNo": "S432",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S432-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §253-d, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S432\n\nSPONSOR: STEWART-COUSINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the expiration of\nthe mortgage recording tax imposed by the city of Yonkers\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend the authorization for the city of\nYonkers to impose a mortgage recording tax until August 31, 2027.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends the tax law to extend the authority of the\ncity of Yonkers to impose an additional mortgage recording tax until\nAugust 31, 2027.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the authority of the city of Yonkers to impose a mort-\ngage recording tax on its residents from August 31, 2025 to August 31,\n2027. Because revenues from the mortgage recording tax are included in\nthe city's budget, this extension is necessary in order to help Yonkers\nmaintain financial stability.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023 - S6822 (Stewart-Cousins); Chapter 179\n\n2020 - S7508B (Budget); Chapter 58, Part XXX, Subpart E, Item D\n\n2017 - A40001 (Rules); Chapter 61, Part C, Subpart D\n\n2015 - S3878 (Stewart-Cousins); Chapter 22\n\n2013 - S4116 (Stewart-Cousins); Chapter 76\n\n2011 - S2983 (Stewart-Cousins); Chapter 392\n\n2009 - S3334 (Stewart-Cousins); Chapter 142\n\n2007 - S4138 (Stewart-Cousins); Chapter 383\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
